  "id": "memory-decay",
  "term": "memory decay",
  "definition": "Memory decay is the gradual weakening of a memory trace over time, such as in short-lasting sensory memory. Its rate can vary depending on the properties of the stimulus and on prior language experience or long-term memory representations.",
